{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>חוצץ</b> — a participle, like יורד, like 'חדשיו חוצצו' (his months came forth), meaning they gathered and assembled, in the manner of 'כי מלאו ימי' (for my days are completed); and likewise 'ויצא חוצץ' — it went out assembled and gathered, in the manner of 'אסף החסיל' (the locust has gathered). Another interpretation: from חצצון תמר."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the unusual word חוצץ in Proverbs 30:27. The verse citations are left implicit by Ibn Ezra (no chapter/verse numbers given); 'כי מלאו ימי' likely echoes Genesis 29:21 phrasing and 'ויצא חוצץ' may refer to Judges 5:14 'מחוצץ' which Ibn Ezra reads as from this root. 'חצצון תמר' is 'Hatzatzon-Tamar' (2 Chronicles 20:2). The phrase 'כמו יורד' is cryptic and may be textually uncertain; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:43.958459821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}